{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyGarnirFactor"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.exists_garnir_murphyMRow_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.exists_garnir_murphyMRow_factor","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyRefTab.lean#L203-L236","doc":"**Mathas 3.13, on Mathas' Murphy element.**\n\nA row-standard non-standard `t` gives a Garnir tableau `g` and a `w` with\n\n    m^row_{s t}  =  m^row_{s g} · T_w\n\nThis is 3.14's rewriting step, on the object 3.14 is about.  It does **not** hold for the\ncolumn-superstandard `murphyM` — see the module docstring; that is why the reference had to\nbecome a parameter first. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.murphyMRef_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.murphyMRef_smul","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyRefTab.lean#L180-L191","doc":"**`m^r_{s, w • g} = m^r_{s, g} · T_w`** on a length-additive factorisation, for every\nreference `r`.  `MurphyGarnirFactor.murphyM_smul` is the `colSuperstandard` case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.Tw_dAtRef_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.Tw_dAtRef_smul","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyRefTab.lean#L164-L178","doc":"**`T_{d_r(w • g)} = T_{d_r(g)} · T_w`** when the lengths add.\n\nThe `T_w` is on the **right** — the flipped handedness of `Tw_mul_Tw`, which is the side\n`m_{st}` needs since `T_{d(t)}` is its rightmost factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.murphyMRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.murphyMRow","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyRefTab.lean#L151-L157","doc":"**Mathas' Murphy element**: the row-superstandard instance.  This is the object 3.13\nand 3.14 are about, and the one `exists_garnir_murphyMRow_factor` below factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.murphyMRef_colSuperstandard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.murphyMRef_colSuperstandard","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyRefTab.lean#L142-L149","doc":"**`murphyM` is the column-superstandard instance** — definitionally, so nothing\ndownstream of `murphyM` is disturbed by this file's existence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.murphyMRef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.murphyMRef","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyRefTab.lean#L132-L140","doc":"**Murphy's `m_{st}`, with the reference tableau explicit**:\n`T*_{d_r(s)} · x_r · T_{d_r(t)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.dAtRef_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.dAtRef_smul","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyRefTab.lean#L118-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.dAtRef_refTab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.dAtRef_refTab","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyRefTab.lean#L113-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.dAtRef_colSuperstandard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.dAtRef_colSuperstandard","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyRefTab.lean#L108-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.dAtRef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.dAtRef","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyRefTab.lean#L103-L106","doc":"`d_r(t)` at the Hecke algebra's index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.dOfRef_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.dOfRef_smul","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyRefTab.lean#L90-L101","doc":"**The factorisation is reference-insensitive.**  `d_r(w • g) = w · d_r(g)` for *every*\nreference — one proof, where the corpus had two (`TableauPerm.dOf_smul` and\n`MurphyGarnirFactor.HeckeMurphyYoung_dOf_smul`) and no statement connecting them.\n\nThis is the half that transfers.  The half that does not is length additivity, and that is\nwhat forces `murphyMRow` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.dOfRef_refTab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.dOfRef_refTab","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyRefTab.lean#L87-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.dOfRef_colSuperstandard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.dOfRef_colSuperstandard","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyRefTab.lean#L83-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.dOfRef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MurphyRefTab.dOfRef","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MurphyRefTab.lean#L75-L81","doc":"**`d_r(t)`** — the permutation carrying an arbitrary reference tableau `r` to `t`.\n\n`HeckeMurphyYoung.dOf` is this at `r = colSuperstandard μ` and `TableauPerm.dOf` at\n`r = refTab μ`; both are `rfl` instances (`dOfRef_colSuperstandard`, `dOfRef_refTab`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}